comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-05T21:28:26.924Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-05: searched all statuses for GH-912, GH-688, atomic cross-owner seeded Plan creation, ownership conflict, and partial Plan persistence. pm-96tter is the completed original fix; this item records the newly reproduced regression. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/912"
  "2026-08-06T06:53:55.342Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: Plan creation now performs base create under the resolved author, then seeds Plan metadata and transfers the requested assignee in the same governed mutation. Strict cross-owner regression, strict full-metadata CLI/SDK regression, rollback regression, manual fresh-workspace proof, build, static gates, and 6,887-test exact 100/100/100/100 coverage all pass."
  "2026-08-06T06:55:34.147Z","harness:codex","Delivery: PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/916 at exact head 0a06ef07f37d6b0b5f07d0e108d9e73b8da24910."
  "2026-08-06T07:25:39.605Z","harness:codex","Exact-head delivery evidence: PR #916 head fea4ba930cd0d1e42766510a3c4088942c2716f3 passed every hosted runner/check, including merged exact coverage, static/docstrings, Windows, compatibility, smokes, CodeQL, Trivy, TruffleHog, Semgrep, Codecov, benchmarks, and platform runtimes. Sourcery's architecture guide and Codecov/CodSpeed reports had no actionable findings and were acknowledged with contextual replies. CodeRabbit and the formal Sourcery review were rate/quota limited; each artifact was down-voted and replied to, and is recorded as a limitation rather than approval. Greptile produced no review artifact after repeated exact-head triggers."
